# Step 28, the arguments of an extension's program on Windows: what a
# batch script is never given, a .exe's arguments in the C runtime's
# quotes, and the characters a code page's best fit makes a quote or a
# backslash, refused on every system (docs/architecture/12-extensions.md,
# "Windows").
#
# The breaks marked `os: windows` are judged by the Windows tests; run them
# on a runner with `gh workflow run try --ref <branch> -f os=windows
# -f command="mutate step-28-winargs --jobs 2"`.

# ------------------------------------------- what a script is never given

[break] shim-ampersand-taken
rule: An argument with an ampersand is refused for a batch script: a script that reads the argument again runs what follows it.
file: crates/cineris-core/src/programs.rs
in: REFUSED
find: ('&', "an ampersand (&)")
replace: ('\u{1}', "an ampersand (&)")
caught-by:
    cineris-core programs::tests::each_character_cmd_cannot_carry_is_refused_with_its_name

[break] shim-vertical-bar-taken
rule: An argument with a vertical bar is refused for a batch script: a script that reads the argument again pipes into what follows it.
file: crates/cineris-core/src/programs.rs
in: REFUSED
find: ('|', "a vertical bar (|)")
replace: ('\u{1}', "a vertical bar (|)")
caught-by:
    cineris-core programs::tests::each_character_cmd_cannot_carry_is_refused_with_its_name

[break] shim-less-than-taken
rule: An argument with a less-than sign is refused for a batch script: a script that reads the argument again redirects its input.
file: crates/cineris-core/src/programs.rs
in: REFUSED
find: ('<', "a less-than sign (<)")
replace: ('\u{1}', "a less-than sign (<)")
caught-by:
    cineris-core programs::tests::each_character_cmd_cannot_carry_is_refused_with_its_name

[break] shim-greater-than-taken
rule: An argument with a greater-than sign is refused for a batch script: a script that reads the argument again writes a file.
file: crates/cineris-core/src/programs.rs
in: REFUSED
find: ('>', "a greater-than sign (>)")
replace: ('\u{1}', "a greater-than sign (>)")
caught-by:
    cineris-core programs::tests::each_character_cmd_cannot_carry_is_refused_with_its_name

[break] shim-caret-taken
rule: An argument with a caret is refused for a batch script: a script that reads the argument again escapes with it, or joins its next line at one at the end.
file: crates/cineris-core/src/programs.rs
in: REFUSED
find: ('^', "a caret (^)")
replace: ('\u{1}', "a caret (^)")
caught-by:
    cineris-core programs::tests::each_character_cmd_cannot_carry_is_refused_with_its_name

[break] shim-opening-parenthesis-taken
rule: An argument with an opening parenthesis is refused for a batch script: a script that reads the argument again inside a block groups at it.
file: crates/cineris-core/src/programs.rs
in: REFUSED
find: ('(', "an opening parenthesis")
replace: ('\u{1}', "an opening parenthesis")
caught-by:
    cineris-core programs::tests::each_character_cmd_cannot_carry_is_refused_with_its_name

[break] shim-closing-parenthesis-taken
rule: An argument with a closing parenthesis is refused for a batch script: a script that reads the argument again inside a block ends the block at it.
file: crates/cineris-core/src/programs.rs
in: REFUSED
find: (')', "a closing parenthesis")
replace: ('\u{1}', "a closing parenthesis")
caught-by:
    cineris-core programs::tests::each_character_cmd_cannot_carry_is_refused_with_its_name

[break] shim-operators-taken-on-windows
rule: A batch script is never given & | < > ^ ( ): one that takes an argument's quotes off and reads it again (set A=%~1, then echo %A%) runs what follows an ampersand.
file: crates/cineris-core/src/programs.rs
in: REFUSED
find: ('&', "an ampersand (&)"), ('|', "a vertical bar (|)"), ('<', "a less-than sign (<)"), ('>', "a greater-than sign (>)"), ('^', "a caret (^)"), ('(', "an opening parenthesis"), (')', "a closing parenthesis")
replace: ('\u{2}', "an ampersand (&)"), ('\u{3}', "a vertical bar (|)"), ('\u{4}', "a less-than sign (<)"), ('\u{5}', "a greater-than sign (>)"), ('\u{6}', "a caret (^)"), ('\u{7}', "an opening parenthesis"), ('\u{8}', "a closing parenthesis")
os: windows
caught-by:
    cineris-core::it ext_exec::windows::each_character_a_shim_cannot_carry_is_refused_with_its_name
    cineris-core::it ext_exec::windows::sys_a_script_that_expands_an_argument_again_is_never_given_an_operator

# ------------------------------------- a .exe's arguments, in the CRT's quotes

[break] exe-arguments-left-to-the-standard-quoting
rule: On Windows a .exe is given every argument in double quotes by the C runtime's rules, never by the standard library's quoting, which leaves * bare.
file: crates/cineris-core/src/programs.rs
in: command_line
find: line.verbatim(crt_quoted(argument))
replace: line.arg(argument.clone())
caught-by:
    cineris-core programs::tests::a_batch_script_is_started_through_cmd_and_a_program_as_it_is
    cineris-core programs::tests::an_exes_arguments_are_quoted_by_the_c_runtimes_rules

[break] exe-quote-not-escaped
rule: A double quote in a .exe's argument is escaped with an odd run of backslashes, so that it does not end the quoting.
file: crates/cineris-core/src/programs.rs
in: crt_quoted
find: quoted.extend(std::iter::repeat_n('\\', backslashes + 1));
replace: quoted.extend(std::iter::repeat_n('\\', backslashes));
caught-by:
    cineris-core programs::tests::an_exes_arguments_are_quoted_by_the_c_runtimes_rules

[break] exe-backslashes-before-a-quote-not-doubled
rule: The backslashes before a double quote in a .exe's argument are doubled, so that the quote's escape is not read as one of them.
file: crates/cineris-core/src/programs.rs
in: crt_quoted
find: quoted.extend(std::iter::repeat_n('\\', backslashes + 1));
replace: quoted.extend(std::iter::repeat_n('\\', 1));
caught-by:
    cineris-core programs::tests::an_exes_arguments_are_quoted_by_the_c_runtimes_rules

[break] exe-trailing-backslashes-not-doubled
rule: The backslashes at the end of a .exe's argument are doubled, so that the closing quote still closes it.
file: crates/cineris-core/src/programs.rs
in: crt_quoted
find: quoted.extend(std::iter::repeat_n('\\', backslashes));
replace: let _ = backslashes;
caught-by:
    cineris-core programs::tests::an_exes_arguments_are_quoted_by_the_c_runtimes_rules

[break] exe-arguments-left-to-the-standard-quoting-on-windows
rule: On Windows a Cygwin-family program is given every argument in double quotes, so that it expands no pattern: `*` is read as `*`, not as the files of the folder it runs in.
file: crates/cineris-core/src/programs.rs
in: command_line
find: if !windows {
replace: if !windows || cfg!(windows) {
os: windows
caught-by:
    cineris-core::it ext_exec::windows::sys_an_msys_program_reads_a_pattern_as_written

# ------------------------- what a code page's best fit makes a quote or a \

[break] lookalikes-taken
rule: An argument with a character a Windows code page's best fit makes a double quote or a backslash is refused on every system, before anything is asked.
file: crates/cineris-core/src/programs.rs
in: command_line
find: if let Some(refused) = lookalike(arguments) { return Err(refused); }
replace: let _ = lookalike;
caught-by:
    cineris-core programs::tests::a_lookalike_of_a_quote_or_a_backslash_is_refused_on_every_system
    cineris-core::it ext_exec::a_lookalike_of_a_quote_is_refused_before_anything_is_asked

[break] lookalike-fullwidth-quote-taken
rule: An argument with a fullwidth quotation mark (U+FF02) is refused: best fit makes it a double quote.
file: crates/cineris-core/src/programs.rs
in: LOOKALIKES
find: '\u{FF02}'
replace: '\u{1}'
caught-by:
    cineris-core programs::tests::a_lookalike_of_a_quote_or_a_backslash_is_refused_on_every_system

[break] lookalike-fullwidth-backslash-taken
rule: An argument with a fullwidth backslash (U+FF3C) is refused: best fit makes it a backslash.
file: crates/cineris-core/src/programs.rs
in: LOOKALIKES
find: '\u{FF3C}'
replace: '\u{1}'
caught-by:
    cineris-core programs::tests::a_lookalike_of_a_quote_or_a_backslash_is_refused_on_every_system

[break] lookalike-yen-sign-taken
rule: An argument with a yen sign (U+00A5) is refused: code page 932's best fit makes it a backslash.
file: crates/cineris-core/src/programs.rs
in: LOOKALIKES
find: '\u{A5}'
replace: '\u{1}'
caught-by:
    cineris-core programs::tests::a_lookalike_of_a_quote_or_a_backslash_is_refused_on_every_system

[break] lookalike-won-sign-taken
rule: An argument with a won sign (U+20A9) is refused: code page 949's best fit makes it a backslash.
file: crates/cineris-core/src/programs.rs
in: LOOKALIKES
find: '\u{20A9}'
replace: '\u{1}'
caught-by:
    cineris-core programs::tests::a_lookalike_of_a_quote_or_a_backslash_is_refused_on_every_system
